    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T18:00:22Z",
    "body": "Facts from upstream/main b2afd64ed (Codex issue worker, no claim):\n\n- The Theme door no longer holds the line width and the anti-aliasing. They are in the viewport Display menu, group \"Graphics\" (#2818, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/display_menu.rs`).\n- A \"Settings\" button is now in the ribbon top band, near Home and Donate (#2428, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/settings_drop.rs`). It opens a dropdown with one row: \"Check for updates\" (`prefs.json`).\n- \"Show origin names\" is still in the browser pane (`browser_pane.rs`).\n- \"Import tool holders\" is still on the Tool library page. \"Offline only\" is still in the AI Chat.\n\nThe \"Done means\" of this issue is the maintainer's answers to the four questions, then sub-issues. That is a maintainer decision, not code. I did not claim the issue and I did not write code.\n\nA possible direction for the maintainer: make the existing Settings dropdown open the Settings window. The window would then hold \"Check for updates\" too. The maintainer decides.\n",
